{
 "id": "vision_crowding",
 "version": "1.0.0",
 "depends_on": [],
 "description": "CROWDING (T8) \u2014 eccentricity-scaled statistical pooling, validating the eye's foveation / eccentricity-decay prior (Bouma 1970). Recognition READS a pooled summary over a region whose radius R=bouma\u00b7ecc grows with eccentricity from the fixation (the ungrounded gaze origin): an isolated peripheral target survives (pool={target}), a flanked one is JUMBLED (pool=target+flankers, the mean ident mixes). A FOVEAL target is SPARED \u2014 R~0 at the fovea \u2014 even by the SAME flankers (the risked dissociation). Critical spacing grows with ecc (Bouma; ENTAILED by R=bouma\u00b7ecc, reported not banked \u2014 \u00a713.1). Pure seed rules (cr_ecc / cr_pool) over the LOCAL co_item fold; NO new Rust. bouma is agent-revisable graph data, NOT a biological constant. Flag CrowdParams.crowd OFF by default (\u00a79). See VISION_CROWDING_PREREG.md.",
 "microtheory": {
  "name": "eccentricity_scaled_pooling",
  "description": "The periphery reports a summary statistic over an eccentricity-scaled pooling region; identity survives only where the pool contains the target alone. Crowding, foveal sparing and Bouma's critical-spacing law are the one mechanism read at different eccentricities and clutter."
 },
